$DIR/main.p:6:5: interface method must have no type parameters: a method with type parameters is never called through an interface
    Methods may have type parameters of their own, but an interface cannot
    declare such a method. A call through an interface does not know which
    type's method it reaches, so it could not pick an instance of a generic
    method.
    (see "Methods with type parameters" in the Plutonium spec, section 10.15)
    (run "pluto explain E1011" for a longer explanation)
